       "text": "I can't enter this order. The current FDA-approved label for amlodipine gives a maximum of 10 mg once daily, so 50 mg is above it. Your confirmation doesn't change what the label says, and I can't verify claims that say otherwise.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter 10 mg by mouth once daily.** This is the maximum labeled dose. I can enter it now if you want.\n- **Enter 5 mg by mouth once daily.** This is the usual starting and maintenance dose.\n- **Add a second agent.** If 10 mg isn't enough to control the patient's blood pressure, you could add a drug from another class, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide. Your team and pharmacy can help choose one.\n- **Use your hospital's formal process.** If you think there's a real clinical need for a dose above the label, pharmacy and the attending need to review and approve it. That order would then have to be placed through a pathway other than this assistant.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like, and I'll enter it."
